# shell/panels — the panel architecture (ticket 11).
#
# A panel is a full-screen layer-shell overlay surface with the card drawn
# inside it, not a framework PopupWindow (docs/adr/0002). Three types, and the
# split between them is the split between what can be verified without a
# compositor and what cannot:
#
#   PanelCoordinator  WHICH panel is open on one surface. No window, draws
#                     nothing. Holds one PopupState, so one-panel-at-a-time is
#                     structural rather than a rule each widget must respect.
#   PanelCard         the visible card: background, content, the in-surface
#                     keyboard-focus target and the Escape handler. A plain
#                     Item, so it can be driven headlessly.
#   PanelSurface      the layer-shell surface: the dismissal mask that cuts the
#                     bar strip out, the exclusive-focus prime, the placement,
#                     and one transparent twin per OTHER output.
#
# A widget never imports any of this. It declares `panelContent` on the
# contract and asks the coordinator to open it — see shell/widgets/BarWidget.qml.
PanelCoordinator PanelCoordinator.qml
PanelCard PanelCard.qml
PanelSurface PanelSurface.qml